@bg restaurant_night
@show diggy
Saturday. Seven. Diggy shows up in a borrowed blazer that's too short in the sleeves.
Frank: So, Duncan. What does your father do?
Diggy: Not around, sir. My mama works two jobs. I work one. I wait tables at Casa Morales downtown. Cassie's mom's place.
Frank sets his fork down. Something passes over his face. Not disapproval. Memory.
Frank: I bussed tables through college. Hated every minute of it.
Diggy: Yes sir. Ms. Morales runs a tight ship. Friday nights are a war.
Frank laughs. A real one. Vega looks at London and raises one perfect eyebrow.
